{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b28c-5604-75c0-aae6-73b3ca1e890f"},"sequence":55,"recorded_at":1780531400000105,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b28c-751a-7453-a13c-6766905db92b"},"task_id":"01a0b28c-751a-7453-a13c-6766905db92b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b28c-751a-7453-a13c-6766905db92b","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kkh1an/TASK-260830-kkh1an_rework-rev3.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-kkh1an, including TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer.md (still the scope of record for WHAT the leaf owns, but its execution instructions are replaced by this one). Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-kkh1an (implement-terminal-instance-state-machine, the SECOND leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; the final leaf TASK-260830-2056mm follows). Change Request revision 2 was reviewed by RUN-260918-4f5cc1 (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED with NO P1: two P2 production findings, two P2 evidence findings and seven P3. Read TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz first. The reviewer confirms on the exact tree that everything else you claim holds: the shipped harness reproduces 70/70 twice, the ratio re-derives to 72 of 72, the real-kill seam holds and hygiene is clean. Keep all of it. Note also that revision 1 carries NO review verdict — its construction died on a trunk defect since fixed — so there is nothing to look for there.\n3|F1 — make the same-key retry after `status` executable. Today `Bind` refuses unconditionally when it replays a receipt that has no completion, which means a receipt keeps its idempotency key forever and the operation-table recovery column \"status, then same-key retry\" plus create's \"idempotent across controller crash\" are unimplementable as written. Reconcile through the production status entry (or accept a fresh `StatusReport` the caller obtained) and do exactly what the row columns say: replay the recorded result when the target state is proven; continue the SAME operation from the proven source state when nothing happened (for create, absence proven by a successful status read means perform the effects under the same receipt and complete it); and keep refusing `status_first` only while the observation is genuinely unknown. Keep the existing SIGKILL evidence and extend it: crash at the receipt seam, then status, then a same-key retry completes with exactly one result and one instance and no second receipt — and a same-key retry WITHOUT a status read still refuses. Either fix the `StoreHooks` doc sentence or make it true at the engine. Ship a narrowing row per new arm.\n4|F2 — fence the stale incarnation under a remote winner. `ObserveFencing` never fences a stale incarnation whose winner is on another host, which is exactly the force-takeover case the pinned Section 13.3 step 15 exists for. Fix it WITHOUT a local tuple comparison: compose the landed fencing gate, do not fork it. Drive both remote members (older epoch, and same-epoch losing lease) from `active`, `parked` and `quiescing`, and keep the winning-token-under-foreign-host case as \"no transition\". Add narrowing rows.\n5|E1 — create-row negatives at the engine: control lease, expired lease and foreign lease authorization; stale generation; headless-from-`absent` without `headless_creation`; and create's second-effect committed timeout. Each pre-effect case must assert that NO receipt is bound. Re-key the harness rows `N-engine-auth-entry` and `N-engine-generation-entry` so that a mutant exempting `create` is killed — today they pass while create walks through.\n6|E2 — the per-effect recheck is pinned at one position only, and the reported session is never compared in any status test. Rotate the lease and the generation before the THIRD stop effect, and drift the reported session on both status lookup paths (plus each of the other five axes named as P3-5).\n7|P3 — P3-1 a pre-link store failure must restore the source state; P3-2 name the fencing sources or state the bound; P3-3 the deadline instant on both entries; P3-4 add `attach` and `none` to the kind negatives; P3-6 and P3-7 as you judge; and document `holder_host_id` as unbound. Then reword TRACEABILITY rows 70 and 71 and the \"recovers through status\" sentence in the results and LOGBOOK once F1 is in — those sentences are currently true only of the intent, not of the code.\n8|Procedure: your candidate sits on the predecessor checkpoint c61fc06 on a Story branch already refreshed onto c3aae73. Do not refresh unless origin/main actually moves; if it does, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-kkh1an` and audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old base> <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keeping README/LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content. You are a MIDDLE leaf: do NOT touch internal/traceability — the final leaf TASK-260830-2056mm carries the registry bindings and the pin. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured validation suite once (30 commands at trunk c3aae73 — read the count from the candidate config rather than assuming it; command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs). Update TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-kkh1an --role developer` so revision 3 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3 hours in. Report the ratio you MEASURE, not the one you planned.\n9|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: this task has already lost runs to a provider idle timeout and to a trunk defect. If a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n10|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 3.","final_result":true}}}
