{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b28c-5604-75c0-aae6-73b3ca1e890f"},"sequence":57,"recorded_at":1780531400000109,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b28c-74f6-7f72-90ab-5371fb03dc1d"},"task_id":"01a0b28c-74f6-7f72-90ab-5371fb03dc1d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b28c-74f6-7f72-90ab-5371fb03dc1d","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kkh1an/TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-kkh1an (implement-terminal-instance-state-machine), the SECOND leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe (ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding, EPIC M1). Predecessor TASK-260830-1geqhj (the `ax pane` enforcement wrapper decision core) is accepted and checkpointed on the Story branch; the final leaf TASK-260830-2056mm (terminal binding events and recovery) follows you and owns the Story-close items. Implement, as production code, the Terminal Instance lifecycle contract of pinned Section 4.C over the LANDED internal/terminalbackend package — that package already owns `InstanceState`/`ParseInstanceState` (the eight-state closed enum absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable), `Operation`/`ParseOperation`, `SideEffect`/`ParseSideEffect`, `Transition`/`CheckTransition`, `CheckErrorAllowed`, `IdempotencyKey`, `Receipt`/`Ledger`/`ImportLedger`, `StatusResult`/`CheckStatusResult`, `AttachAuthorization`/`CheckAttachRequest`/`CheckAttachResult` and the Manifest/Probe/descriptor admission. Do NOT fork a second state machine or a second enum: extend that package (or add a sibling package that drives it) and state in the results exactly which existing type or gate each addition extends.\n2|Scope of this leaf — the parts of 4.C the landed code does NOT yet model:\n3|(1) AXAuthorization as a closed object (exactly lease_id:UUIDv4, lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991], holder_host_id:UUIDv7 and the remaining members exactly as the pinned section lists them, no extra and no missing member, unknown member refused), parsed through the landed canonicaljson closed-shape discipline, with the epoch bound witnessed at 1, 9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values; today `Transition.Authorization` is only a string, so every operation's authorization requirement must become a checked object.\n4|(2) The closed RetryDisposition enum — exactly replay_same, status_first, new_authorization, required_operator_action — carried by every result, plus the request/result identity contract: every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and idempotency IDs, the exact backend ID/version/generation, a deadline and an expiring AX authorization with the winning lease ID/epoch; every result repeats those identities and adds before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs and exactly one retry disposition.\n5|(3) The state-entry rules, each one driven and each one mutated: `creating` is entered only by `create`, only after its durable idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect; an error BEFORE a side effect restores the source state; an error AFTER an effect whose result cannot be proven moves the local observation to `unavailable` with `status_first` and MUST NOT claim `absent`; no operation other than `quiesce-input` enters `quiescing`; no backend operation enters `stale_fenced` — only AX fencing observation does (drive that from the landed internal/fencing projection, do not invent a second fencing model); authorization AND generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect (not once at entry); a deadline cancels waiting but never a committed effect.\n6|(4) Generation-safe evidence: `backend_generation` is the canonical string[1..256] bound in every containing contract — reject lengths 0 and 257 and accept 256 in the Terminal Instance Binding, the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor, every operation body and the CLI Result 4 summary projection, and make a stale generation refuse with the landed `terminal_backend_stale_generation` class rather than a fresh code.\n7|(5) The operation table rows for status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary and request-stop exactly as pinned: their source→target states, their listed side effects from the closed TerminalBackendSideEffect enum, their exact idempotency key material (UTF-8 `terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation`, `… + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind`, `… + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id`), their evidence kinds (input_quiescence, safe_boundary_observation, provider_process_observation, graceful_stop) and their exact admitted refusal sets — a refusal code outside the row's set must be rejected by `CheckErrorAllowed`, and `status` timeout/read failure is `unknown`, never `absent`.\n8|Tests: every state transition and every refusal row driven through the production entry with positives and negatives; the closed enums pinned as closed (an added, removed or re-spelled member must redden a test, and a member census must count copies, not names); receipt/idempotency replay proving an identical retry replays and a changed operation in-window is `idempotency_mismatch`; crash evidence at the durable receipt seam (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) proving `creating` is never entered before the receipt is durable and that a lost result recovers through `status` rather than `absent`; a narrowing mutant per gate (drop or weaken each recheck, each bound, each disposition mapping) executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control; and a conformance matrix over every 4.C clause. No `ax` CLI, no tmux/ConPTY process control and no provider process — those are modeled callers; state that bound explicitly.\n9|COMMON CONTRACT (non-first, non-final leaf of a Story whose predecessor leaves are already checkpointed). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named above; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260917-110onn) may land on trunk during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) and above all the packages your own predecessor leaf just added on this Story branch — never fork a second model of anything already modeled; extend or adopt, and say in the results which existing type or gate you extended. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and in the conformance matrix instead. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe ALREADY EXISTS and its tip is your predecessor leaf's signed checkpoint commit — do not re-provision it, do not rebase it, do not commit on it, do not amend or revert the checkpoint, and never edit .task-board directly or self-accept. Your candidate is the UNCOMMITTED working tree on top of that checkpoint: exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Before you start, read the predecessor's landed delta (`git -C .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree show --stat HEAD`) and its outcome resources so you extend it instead of restating it. If origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-kkh1an` (LOGBOOK append conflicts are resolved with --replay-resolutions: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add {\"checkpoint_oid\": <the ORIGINAL checkpoint OID recorded before the refresh>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>} keeping every entry newest-first), then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that also appears in your `git status` and restore trunk content by hand — a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies of trunk-changed files into the candidate and they read as reverts (README/LOGBOOK stay purely additive; task-board.config.json must equal HEAD byte-for-byte). Before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite (30 commands as of trunk c3aae73 — STORY-260830-4qojoz added three bounded rpcwire fuzz gates; read the count from the candidate config rather than assuming it) once before handoff (command 5 is `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs — that is expected, do not shorten it; command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted … -check`). Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in — if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md, TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-kkh1an --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.\n10|\n11|REJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\n12|(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\n13|(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\n14|(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\n15|(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\n16|(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\n17|(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \"Composes X\", \"never admits what decoding refuses\", \"nothing re-implemented\", \"no cached sentinel can authorize\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\n18|Finally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and