{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b28c-5604-75c0-aae6-73b3ca1e890f"},"sequence":59,"recorded_at":1780531400000113,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de"},"call_id":"call_01a0b28c6fdf734d9561a2c41dd26398","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kkh1an/TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-kkh1an (implement-terminal-instance-state-machine), the SECOND leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe (ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding, EPIC M1). Predecessor TASK-260830-1geqhj (the `ax pane` enforcement wrapper decision core) is accepted and checkpointed on the Story branch; the final leaf TASK-260830-2056mm (terminal binding events and recovery) follows you and owns the Story-close items. Implement, as production code, the Terminal Instance lifecycle contract of pinned Section 4.C over the LANDED internal/terminalbackend package — that package already owns `InstanceState`/`ParseInstanceState` (the eight-state closed enum absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable), `Operation`/`ParseOperation`, `SideEffect`/`ParseSideEffect`, `Transition`/`CheckTransition`, `CheckErrorAllowed`, `IdempotencyKey`, `Receipt`/`Ledger`/`ImportLedger`, `StatusResult`/`CheckStatusResult`, `AttachAuthorization`/`CheckAttachRequest`/`CheckAttachResult` and the Manifest/Probe/descriptor admission. Do NOT fork a second state machine or a second enum: extend that package (or add a sibling package that drives it) and state in the results exactly which existing type or gate each addition extends.\n2|Scope of this leaf — the parts of 4.C the landed code does NOT yet model:\n3|(1) AXAuthorization as a closed object (exactly lease_id:UUIDv4, lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991], holder_host_id:UUIDv7 and the remaining members exactly as the pinned section lists them, no extra and no missing member, unknown member refused), parsed through the landed canonicaljson closed-shape discipline, with the epoch bound witnessed at 1, 9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values; today `Transition.Authorization` is only a string, so every operation's authorization requirement must become a checked object.\n4|(2) The closed RetryDisposition enum — exactly replay_same, status_first, new_authorization, required_operator_action — carried by every result, plus the request/result identity contract: every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and idempotency IDs, the exact backend ID/version/generation, a deadline and an expiring AX authorization with the winning lease ID/epoch; every result repeats those identities and adds before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs and exactly one retry disposition.\n5|(3) The state-entry rules, each one driven and each one mutated: `creating` is entered only by `create`, only after its durable idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect; an error BEFORE a side effect restores the source state; an error AFTER an effect whose result cannot be proven moves the local observation to `unavailable` with `status_first` and MUST NOT claim `absent`; no operation other than `quiesce-input` enters `quiescing`; no backend operation enters `stale_fenced` — only AX fencing observation does (drive that from the landed internal/fencing projection, do not invent a second fencing model); authorization AND generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect (not once at entry); a deadline cancels waiting but never a committed effect.\n6|(4) Generation-safe evidence: `backend_generation` is the canonical string[1..256] bound in every containing contract — reject lengths 0 and 257 and accept 256 in the Terminal Instance Binding, the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor, every operation body and the CLI Result 4 summary projection, and make a stale generation refuse with the landed `terminal_backend_stale_generation` class rather than a fresh code.\n7|(5) The operation table rows for status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary and request-stop exactly as pinned: their source→target states, their listed side effects from the closed TerminalBackendSideEffect enum, their exact idempotency key material (UTF-8 `terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation`, `… + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind`, `… + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id`), their evidence kinds (input_quiescence, safe_boundary_observation, provider_process_observation, graceful_stop) and their exact admitted refusal sets — a refusal code outside the row's set must be rejected by `CheckErrorAllowed`, and `status` timeout/read failure is `unknown`, never `absent`.\n8|Tests: every state transition and every refusal row driven through the production entry with positives and negatives; the closed enums pinned as closed (an added, removed or re-spelled member must redden a test, and a member census must count copies, not names); receipt/idempotency replay proving an identical retry replays and a changed operation in-window is `idempotency_mismatch`; crash evidence at the durable receipt seam (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) proving `creating` is never entered before the receipt is durable and that a lost result recovers through `status` rather than `absent`; a narrowing mutant per gate (drop or weaken each recheck, each bound, each disposition mapping) executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control; and a conformance matrix over every 4.C clause. No `ax` CLI, no tmux/ConPTY process control and no provider process — those are modeled callers; state that bound explicitly.\n9|COMMON CONTRACT (non-first, non-final leaf of a Story whose predecessor leaves are already checkpointed). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named above; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260917-110onn) may land on trunk during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) and above all the packages your own predecessor leaf just added on this Story branch — never fork a second model of anything already modeled; extend or adopt, and say in the results which existing type or gate you extended. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and in the conformance matrix instead. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree .temp/STORY