{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b28c-5604-75c0-aae6-73b3ca1e890f"},"sequence":320,"recorded_at":1780531400000635,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b28d-5521-7370-8cb9-d8bc2fd97778"},"task_id":"01a0b28d-5521-7370-8cb9-d8bc2fd97778","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b28d-5521-7370-8cb9-d8bc2fd97778","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/kkh1an-rev2/TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-kkh1an — independent review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-kkh1an-2 revision 2\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED (routed `to-dev`).** No P1. Two P2 production\n4|findings on the lifecycle contract itself (F1: an interrupted attempt poisons\n5|its idempotency key forever, so the row recovery column \"status, then same-key\n6|retry\" and create's \"idempotent across controller crash\" are unimplementable;\n7|F2: `ObserveFencing` never fences a stale incarnation whose winner is on\n8|another host — the force-takeover case §13.3 step 15 exists for), two P2\n9|evidence findings (E1: the create row's authorization/generation/headless\n10|gates have no negative test at the engine; E2: the per-effect recheck is pinned\n11|at one position and the reported session is never compared in any status test)\n12|and seven P3 items. Everything else the producer claims holds on the exact\n13|tree: the shipped harness reproduces 70/70 twice, the ratio re-derives to\n14|72 of 72, the real-kill seam holds, hygiene is clean.\n15|\n16|Reviewer: RUN-260918-4f5cc1 (claude-opus-5 max). Reviewed bytes: base\n17|`c61fc06ad8190a73c3005e137282829936dac970` (the predecessor checkpoint, = the\n18|Story branch tip), candidate tree `b605cc51c9dee44bc90f90d950892a58b09571ca`\n19|(recomputed from the live Story worktree with a temporary untracked-aware index:\n20|equal), patch sha256\n21|`bf88c269de2bece432ded49c931c2d763cd82788b2f9b6c1eecc12323fe2ae52` (equal to the\n22|CR record and to `git diff --binary` of the two OIDs). Every probe ran in\n23|isolated `git archive` copies of the exact tree under\n24|`.temp/TASK-260830-kkh1an/review-rev2/` (`cand/` tree-exact checks, `cand-h/`\n25|shipped harness, `cand-m/` reviewer mutants, `cand-p/` probes and witnesses;\n26|`cand-h`/`cand-m` carry their own `.git` and their post-run `write-tree` equals\n27|the candidate OID; `cand-p` is diffed against `cand/` and differs only by the\n28|three probe files). The live Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never\n29|touched (`git status` after the review: `M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n30|`M internal/axpane/decide.go`, `?? internal/terminstance/` only).\n31|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` everywhere; 0 `__pycache__` in any copy. Every\n32|instrument, raw log and subprocess exit is in\n33|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (paths below are relative to\n34|that archive).\n35|\n36|## 0. Inherited advisories (predecessor P3-1..P3-7), graded\n37|\n38|| Item | Producer disposition | Grade |\n39|| --- | --- | --- |\n40|| P3-1 journal-only restore closure path | Left to TASK-260830-2056mm, stated in TRACEABILITY (\"recovery domain\") and results | Acceptable: explicit, with a reason |\n41|| P3-2 pure core not fail-closed on a missing closure | Bound stated: no I/O-free `Decide` caller in this leaf | Acceptable as a bound (verified: `grep -r \"axpane\\.\" internal/terminstance` = 0 production references) |\n42|| P3-3 remote-owned newest absent locally | Bound stated: no checkpoint loader here | Acceptable as a bound |\n43|| P3-4 `EmitParked` winner binding | Left to 2056mm, stated (\"events domain\") | Acceptable: explicit |\n44|| P3-5 `LoadCheckpoint` absence-vs-failure | Left to 2056mm, stated (\"recovery domain\") | Acceptable: explicit |\n45|| P3-6 reattach carries two instance IDs | Closed by a doc sentence on `Decision.Descriptor` (`internal/axpane/decide.go` +4/−1, comment-only) plus the consumer sentence in `terminstance/doc.go` | Closed (the reviewer offered \"document or rebuild\"; documentation chosen; no code path changed, axpane suite green under `-race`, `logs/70`) |\n46|| P3-7 evidence archive hygiene | `TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`: task-scoped README, 188-entry `MANIFEST.sha256`, 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc`, no foreign task files, raw per-plant logs on BOTH passes (70+70) | Closed |\n47|\n48|Nothing was silently dropped.\n49|\n50|## 1. What holds (verified myself on the exact tree)\n51|\n52|| Check | Result | Evidence |\n53|| --- | --- | --- |\n54|| gofmt / go vet / go build; GOOS=linux and GOOS=windows builds; GOOS=windows vet of the package | all exit 0 | `logs/02` |\n55|| `go test ./internal/terminstance -count=1 -v` | exit 0, 168 `--- PASS`, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP | `logs/01` |\n56|| `go test ./... -count=1` (command 4 without `-v`) on the exact tree, rerun by me | exit 0, 40/40 packages `ok` | `logs/04` |\n57|| `-race` on terminstance, axpane, terminalbackend, fencing; `-cover` terminstance 83.8% | all `ok` | `logs/70` |\n58|| tracecheck (registry untouched: contracts=64, clauses 56/569 — trunk figures) / `cataloggen -adopted … -check` / `git diff --check` | exit 0 / 0 / 0 | `logs/70` |\n59|| CR construction suite | runtime-recorded `required=30 green=30 failed=0 missing=0` on the exact tree (accepted from the attached `_rev2-validation.log`; the race gate and fuzz gates were not rerun by me) | resource |\n60|| Shipped harness, isolated pristine copy, two full passes with raw per-plant output | 70/70 both passes (68 narrowing KILLED + 1 tightening KILLED + control SURVIVED), verdict lists identical, 70 raw logs per pass, tree OID equal to the candidate after each pass | `logs/40-harness-pass{1,2}.log`, `logs/mutants-pass{1,2}/` |\n61|| Producer real-kill test `TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates` ×2; my own real SIGKILL at the ENGINE `BeforeEffect` seam of `create` ×2 (receipt durable, no completion, no effect ran, the retry never invents absence, status reads absence) | PASS ×2; my seam holds ×2 for the durability half (the liveness half is F1) | `logs/70`, `logs/60` |\n62|| Ratio | 72 data rows counted in `TRACEABILITY.md`; 70 distinct top-level tests all present in `go test -list` and all `--- PASS` in my verbose run; 7 cited subtests all PASS; rows 53/54 are cross-references to rows 26/36/39/43/49/50 | `logs/82` |\n63|| Spec fidelity (§4.C extracted and diffed): eight-state enum, ten-operation enum, side-effect enum, transition matrix, allowed-error sets, key shapes all landed (`terminalbackend`) and composed, never re-spelled; `AXAuthorization` closed 7-member set with unknown/missing/frame refusals; epoch bound witnessed at 1, 9007199254740991, 0, 9007199254740992 at `ParseAXAuthorization` (committed) and through the nested `MutationContext` surface (my `TestRV2_EpochBoundThroughNestedContext`); `RetryDisposition` closed 4 with a copy-counting AST census plus the behavioural parse pin; `ProviderProofKind` closed 3; `AuthorizationKind` closed 4; exact key material literals asserted (`/quiesce/`, `/boundary/…/<kind>`, `/stop/`, `session/bootstrap`); refusal sets through the landed `CheckErrorAllowed` with in-set and outside-set codes per row; status timeout/read failure → error with no report, never absent; every engine result path carries exactly one of the four literal dispositions (my `TestRV2_EveryResultCarriesExactlyOneLiteralDisposition`) | holds | `logs/12` |\n64|| Generation bound: 0/256/257 (and 256/257 multibyte, chars not bytes) refused/admitted with the landed `terminal_backend_stale_generation` class on the context document, the status body, the Go-level twin and the landed `GenerationDigest`; Binding object and CLI Result 4 stated as bounds (no landed surface — verified: `canonicaljson` rejects the binding URN, `internal/cliresult` carries no raw generation member) | holds | `logs/12` (`TestRV2_DescriptorGenerationBoundLanded`) |\n65|| Composition: `fencing.Authorize`/`ParkDetails`, `terminalbackend.CheckTransition/CheckErrorAllowed/CheckOperation/CheckStatusResult/IdempotencyKey/GenerationDigest/CheckVersionTuple/ParseID`, `environ.DecodeStrictObject/Check*`, `scalar.Parse*` — no second enum, no second fencing comparison, no second JSON discipline. `kindFor` restates the landed (unexported) `Transition.Authorization` column (P3-6 below). | holds | source read |\n66|| Bounds and hygiene: changed paths = exactly the 31 candidate paths; `internal/traceability` untouched; `task-board.config.json` equal to base; README +47/−0 with test and harness commands and the explicit \"no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, no runtime capability claim\"; LOGBOOK +12/−0 newest-first; 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the tree; `os/exec`/`syscall`/`tmux`/ConPTY appear in production only inside the two stated-bound comments | holds | `logs/80` |\n67|\n68|## 2. Coverage statement\n69|\n70|Producer claim: 72 of 72 rows driven. Re-derived: 72 data rows, every named\n71|test and subtest exists and passed (`logs/82`). **I measure 72 of 72 driven**\n72|at the named production entries. Two rows' prose outruns what the tests show:\n73|row 71 (\"… status recovery\") and the results' \"a lost result recovers through\n74|`status`\" — status recovers the *observation*; the *operation* never recovers\n75|(F1). Row 46 (\"stale_fenced only via fencing observation\") is driven on the\n76|local-winner arms only; the remote-winner member of the class is not fenced\n77|(F2). Rows 43/48/49/69 are driven on one operation or one effect position; the\n78|class is not closed (E1, E2).\n79|\n80|## 3. Findings\n81|\n82|No P1: the eight-state enum, the operation/effect vocabularies and the\n83|transition matrix are the landed ones; no second state machine exists.\n84|\n85|### P2 — production\n86|\n87|- **F1 (P2). An interrupted attempt poisons its idempotency key forever; the\n88|  row recovery column cannot be executed.** `ExecuteMutating` (`execute.go:275-284`)\n89|  treats a bound receipt without a completion as `terminal_backend_unavailable`\n90|  / `unavailable` / `status_first` on *every* subsequent same-key request, and\n91|  no production entry (`Engine`, `ReceiptStore`) can move a key out of that\n92|  state. §4.C request-stop row: \"lost result requires `status`, **then same-key\n93|  retry only if not closed**\"; create row: \"identical retry replays it;\n94|  uncertainty requires `status`\"; closing paragraph: \"Create is idempotent on\n95|  (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) **across controller crash** and lost\n96|  result … Identical retry returns the one result/instance\"; §13.13\n97|  `safe_retry`: \"the same logical operation can continue … using every\n98|  caller-stable operation ID … A retry MUST reconcile an uncertain external\n99|  effect before issuing it again and MUST NOT allocate another process\". Driven\n100|  witnesses (`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go`, `probes/zz_review2_crash_unix_test.go`,\n101|  `logs/12`, `logs/60`): (a) quiesce-input receipt without completion →\n102|  retry refuses → `ExecuteStatus` proves `active` (nothing happened) →\n103|  same-key retry **still refuses** `terminal_backend_unavailable at idempotency\n104|  result uncertain`; (b) request-stop receipt without completion → status proves\n105|  `quiescing` (not closed) → same-key retry still refuses; (c) **real\n106|  SIGKILL** of the engine at the `BeforeEffect` seam of `create` (child killed\n107|  by SIGKILL, receipt durable, no completion, no effect ran) → status proves\n108|  `absent` → the identical create retry still refuses ×2 — the\n109|  `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` key can never produce \"the one\n110|  result/instance\"; (d) the `StoreHooks.AfterCommit` error path: `store.go`\n111|  documents \"a hook error propagates to the caller but the receipt stands, so\n112|  the identical retry replays it\" — through the engine the identical retry\n113|  refuses uncertain (`TestRV2_HookErrorThenIdenticalRetryDoesNotReplayThroughEngine`).\n114|  The only exit a caller has is a *new* key (new `quiescence_generation` /\n115|  new `bootstrap_operation_id`), which is exactly the second-allocation §13.13\n116|  forbids when the interrupted attempt may have started a wrapper. The\n117|  durability half (receipt before first effect, never inventing absence) is\n118|  correct and pinned; the liveness half is absent and undeclared (no stated\n119|  bound names it; TRACEABILITY rows 70/71 and LOGBOOK F2 describe the refusal\n120|  as \"the honest interrupted state\" without the resumption).\n121|- **F2 (P2). `ObserveFencing` does not fence a stale incarnation whose winner\n122|  is on another host.** `fencing.go:41-48` keys the transition on\n123|  `ParkStaleOwner` only, but the landed `fencing.Authorize` (gate.go, restore\n124|  is launch-class) evaluates the remote-owner arm *before* the epoch/lease\n125|  arms (\"the operative fact beats the credential: a stale token under a remote\n126|  winner parks remote, it does not report stale\"). So a local epoch-1\n127|  incarnation observed under an epoch-2 winner held by another host — the\n128|  force takeover §13.3 step 15 describes (\"its winning lease fences the prior\n129|  owner logically\") and §13.4 (\"If a higher or winning same-epoch lease is\n130|  observed, the wrapper MUST block input, park or terminate its stale\n131|  provider … and return `stale_owner`\") — returns `(current, false,\n132|  park remote_owner)` from `active`, `parked` and `quiescing`, and the\n133|  same-epoch losing lease under a remote holder does the same\n134|  (`TestRV2_StaleTokenUnderRemoteWinnerIsNotFenced`,\n135|  `TestRV2_SameEpochLosingLeaseUnderRemoteWinnerIsNotFenced`, `logs/12`). The\n136|  local-winner arms fence (control `TestRV2_StaleTokenUnderLocalWinnerFences`\n137|  passes; the committed `TestObserveFencingStaleEpochFences` /\n138|  `…LeaseMismatchFences` use a local holder). Consequences: the prior owner's\n139|  Terminal Instance never reaches `stale_fenced` after a cross-host takeover,\n140|  so the `terminate-stale` row (`stale_fenced|unavailable → stopped`, final\n141|  leaf) cannot target it from that state, and the committed\n142|  `TestObserveFencingNonStaleLeavesState/remote` pins the *winning* token under\n143|  a foreign local host — a different member (not stale) — so the suite reads\n144|  \"remote leaves state\" as if it covered this case. Input stays blocked by the\n145|  landed input gate (`not_owner`), so this is a wrong projection, not an\n146|  admitted mutation. The fix must not compare tuples locally (a second fencing\n147|  model): either derive staleness from the landed gate with the observation's\n148|  own host as the local host (authorize against `LocalHostID = Winner.HolderHostID`\n149|  to ask \"is this token stale relative to the winner\", then read the park), or\n150|  land an exported \"is this token stale\" verdict in `internal/fencing` first.\n151|\n152|### P2 — evidence\n153|\n154|- **E1 (P2). The create row's gates have positive-path-only evidence at the\n155|  engine.** Whole-suite reviewer mutants (`probes/review2_mutants.py`,\n156|  `logs/50-rv2-mutants-pass{1,2}.log`, raw per-plant logs in\n157|  `logs/rv2-mutants-pass{1,2}/`, two passes with identical verdicts; instrument\n158|  proven by the known-killed control `RV2-K` KILLED ×2, the build-break control\n159|  reporting `build broke` ×2 and the comment control SURVIVED ×2):\n160|  `RV2-M8` (entry authorization gate exempts exactly `create`) **SURVIVED ×2**,\n161|  `RV2-M7` (entry generation gate exempts `create`) **SURVIVED ×2**,\n162|  `RV2-M10` (headless_creation conditional skipped for a headless create from\n163|  `absent`) **SURVIVED ×2**, `RV2-M5` (disposition mapping collapsed at the\n164|  engine for a committed `terminal_backend_timeout`, reachable only through\n165|  create's second effect) **SURVIVED ×2**. Witnesses (`logs/rv2-witness-under-mutant/`,\n166|  each PASS pristine / FAIL under its mutant): under M8 a create presented\n167|  with a control-kind, an expired or a foreign-lease authorization **binds a\n168|  durable receipt** before the pre-first-effect recheck refuses it — which, by\n169|  F1, poisons the `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` key; under M7 the same\n170|  for a stale generation; under M10 a headless create from `absent` proceeds\n171|  without `headless_creation`; under M5 create's second-effect timeout reports\n172|  `replay_same` with `after=unavailable`. The committed pins\n173|  (`TestExecutePreEffectErrorsRestoreSource`, harness rows\n174|  `N-engine-auth-entry`/`N-engine-generation-entry`, both keyed on the quiesce\n175|  fixture's operation ID) cover the quiesce row only; `TestExecuteCreateReceiptRule`\n176|  drives the headless conditional from `stopped` only. DoD: \"Gating …\n177|  authorizing … behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate\n178|  admits what it must reject\" is not met for the create row.\n179|- **E2 (P2). The per-effect recheck is pinned at one position, and the\n180|  reported session is never compared.** `RV2-M1` (auth recheck skipped exactly\n181|  before the THIRD effect) and `RV2-M2` (generation recheck skipped before the\n182|  third effect) **SURVIVED ×2**: under a lease rotated at the fourth\n183|  `CurrentLease` read, `request-stop` commits `backend_store_closed`\n184|  unauthorized and reports `stopped`/`replay_same` (witness\n185|  `TestRV2W_M1_LeaseRotatesBeforeThirdEffect`); the committed\n186|  `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect` rotates at the third read only (the\n187|  recheck before effect 2). \"Rechecked immediately before **each** side\n188|  effect\" is a headline AC item (3). `RV2-M15` (session-scoped status lookup\n189|  skips the reported-session comparison) **SURVIVED ×2**: a backend reporting\n190|  ANOTHER session's instance with `identity_match:true` is adopted as this\n191|  session's status (`TestRV2W_M15_SessionScopedForeignSessionRefuses`, pristine\n192|  refuses `status identity binding`); no committed test drifts the reported\n193|  session on either lookup path (`TestExecuteStatusReportMemberRefusals/session`\n194|  uses a malformed value, refused at the grammar).\n195|\n196|### P3\n197|\n198|- **P3-1 Pre-link receipt-store failure moves the observation to\n199|  `unavailable`.** `execute.go:266-274`: any uncoded `Bind` error → `after =\n200|  unavailable`, `terminal_backend_process_failed`, `status_first`. With the\n201|  pending directory read-only (stage fails before any link, nothing durable,\n202|  nothing attempted) the result is `unavailable` (`TestRV2_PreLinkStoreFailureMovesToUnavailable`,\n203|  `logs/12`). §4.C: \"An error before a side effect restores the source state.\"\n204|  Over-strict direction; the receipt is not a side effect. Distinguish the\n205|  pre-link failures (restore source) from the post-link ones (hook error,\n206|  directory sync — genuinely uncertain).\n207|- **P3-2 `ObserveFencing` fences from `absent`, `stopped`, `creating` and\n208|  `unavailable`** (`TestRV2_ObserveFencingFencesFromAbsentAndStopped`): an\n209|  incarnation that does not exist becomes `stale_fenced`, and a\n210|  `terminate-stale` (final leaf) would then target nothing. Bound the sources\n211|  (the live states) or state the bound.\n212|- **P3-3 Deadline instant admitted by no test.** `RV2-M3` (entry deadline\n213|  `!Before` → `After`, admits `now == deadline_at`) and `RV2-M4` (same at\n214|  `ExecuteStatus`) SURVIVED ×2; under M3 a receipt is bound for a request whose\n215|  deadline has arrived, under M4 status proceeds at the instant. The committed\n216|  deadline tests use an hour past the deadline. Add the instant to\n217|  `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes` and a status-deadline test.\n218|- **P3-4 `ParseAuthorizationKind` admits the landed sibling name `attach`\n219|  under a narrowing (`RV2-M6` SURVIVED ×2).** The committed non-members are\n220|  `admin`, `CREATE`, `\"\"`, `force-stale`; the AST census inspects case clauses\n221|  only, so an `if value == \"attach\"` in the default arm is invisible to it.\n222|  Add `attach` and `none` (the two landed transition-table kinds that are not\n223|  AXAuthorization kinds) to the negative corpus.\n224|- **P3-5 identity_match six-way conjunction pinned on the generation axis\n225|  only.** `RV2-M9` (drop the implementation conjunct) SURVIVED ×2; a lying\n226|  match with only the implementation version drifted is adopted. My\n227|  `TestRV2_StatusIdentityMatchEachAxis` drives all five axes both ways on the\n228|  pristine tree (all pass): commit it or its equivalent.\n229|- **P3-6 `kindFor` restates the landed `Transition.Authorization` column.**\n230|  The landed table is unexported, so the sibling package re-spells\n231|  create→create, quiesce/wait/stop→control. Pinned by `N-engine-kind-map`, but a\n232|  drift between the two tables is invisible. An exported accessor in\n233|  `terminalbackend` (or extending that package) removes the twin.\n234|- **P3-7 `unavailable` paired with `new_authorization`.** A lease rotation\n235|  after a committed effect returns `after=unavailable` with\n236|  `new_authorization` (`TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect/lease_rotates_mid-operation`,\n237|  pinned; harness `N-disp-unauthorized`). §4.C's only sentence about\n238|  `unavailable` pairs it with `status_first`; the leaf's per-code mapping is\n239|  its own contract (stated), so this is recorded as a literal tension, not a\n240|  defect: the caller that lost the lease cannot act on `new_authorization`\n241|  without a status read either.\n242|\n243|### Characterizations (not findings)\n244|\n245|- The replay path is reachable only from the original source state: an\n246|  identical retry presented from the post-transition state refuses\n247|  `local_precondition_failed` at the landed `CheckTransition` before the\n248|  receipt is read (`TestRV2_ReplayRequiresOriginalSource`). Consistent with the\n249|  lost-result model (the caller never observed the transition).\n250|- `holder_host_id` is parsed (UUIDv7) and never bound: `LeaseView` carries\n251|  `(lease_id, epoch)` only, which is the §5.3 winning tuple; a foreign holder\n252|  under the winning tuple is admitted (`TestRV2_HolderHostIDIsUnboundAtCheckAuthorization`).\n253|  Not a spec violation; worth a stated bound.\n254|- `N-auth-epoch-high` is a tightening row, documented as such; the min edge,\n255|  the delegate's own uint53 ceiling (`environ`) and the four-value witness\n256|  triangulate the bound. Accepted.\n257|\n258|## 4. DoD walk (live merged checklist)\n259|\n260|Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable — partially: the\n261|rows, gates, receipts and rechecks exist; the recovery column (F1) and the\n262|remote-winner fencing member (F2) do not. Positive/negative/compatibility/\n263|recovery tests pass with logs — yes for what is committed. README/traceability\n264|without unsupported claims — README yes; TRACEABILITY/results \"recovers\n265|through status\" outruns the behaviour (F1). Uncommitted in the Story worktree\n266|— yes (tree OID equal). Ratio — 72 of 72 with call sites. Negative tests that\n267|fail when the gate admits — not for the create row (E1). Narrowing mutant per\n268|gate — shipped 69 KILLED ×2; eleven reviewer narrowings SURVIVED ×2 with\n269|non-equivalent witnesses (E1, E2, P3-3/4/5). No source-text gate in production\n270|(the AST census is a test instrument, not a gate; its blind spot is P3-4).\n271|Lint/build — clean. Outcome artifacts — attached and hygienic. Logbook —\n272|newest-first, additive. Implementation matches AC — no (F1, F2). Fits the\n273|architecture — yes (composition over the landed owners; P3-6). Tests green —\n274|yes. Gates attacked, not read — yes, and the attack found the gaps above.\n275|\n276|## 5. Instruments (all in the evidence archive)\n277|\n278|`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go` (15 probes: 6 CHARACTERIZATION failures =\n279|F1 ×3, F2 ×2, P3-1 ×1; the other 9 PASS) plus `TestRV2_RealKillAtFirstEffectSeam`\n280|in `probes/zz_review2_crash_unix_test.go` (F1 ×1 with a real SIGKILL; 26\n281|top-level RV2 tests in all: 19 PASS, 7 CHARACTERIZATION FAIL, `logs/12`), `probes/zz_review2_witness_test.go` (10 delta witnesses, all PASS\n282|pristine, each FAIL under its mutant), `probes/review2_mutants.py` (11\n283|narrowing rows + 3 controls, whole-suite killer, raw per-plant logs with\n284|exits), `probes/review2_witness_runner.py`, `logs/01`, `02`, `04`, `10`–`12`\n285|(probes), `40` + `mutants-pass{1,2}/` (shipped harness ×2), `50` +\n286|`rv2-mutants-pass{1,2}/` (reviewer mutants ×2), `51` + `rv2-witness-under-mutant/`\n287|(witness under each mutant), `60` (real kill ×2), `70` (tree-exact checks),\n288|`80` (hygiene), `82` (ratio), `REVIEW-MANIFEST.txt` (sha256 of every file).\n289|\n290|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n291|\n292|1. **F1 — make the same-key retry after `status` executable.** When\n293|   `Bind` replays a receipt that has no completion, do not refuse\n294|   unconditionally: reconcile through the production status entry (or accept a\n295|   fresh `StatusReport` the caller obtained) and, exactly as the row columns\n296|   say, replay the recorded result when the target state is proven, continue\n297|   the same operation from the proven source state when nothing happened\n298|   (create: absence proven by a successful status read → perform the effects\n299|   under the same receipt and complete it), and keep refusing `status_first`\n300|   only while the observation is genuinely unknown. Keep the SIGKILL evidence\n301|   and add the resumption to it: crash at the receipt seam → status → same-key\n302|   retry completes with one result/instance and no second receipt; a same-key\n303|   retry WITHOUT a status read still refuses. Fix the `StoreHooks` doc sentence\n304|   or make it true at the engine. Add a narrowing row per new arm.\n305|2. **F2 — fence the stale incarnation under a remote winner** without a local\n306|   tuple comparison (compose the landed gate; do not fork it). Drive both\n307|   remote members (older epoch, same-epoch losing lease) from `active`,\n308|   `parked` and `quiescing`; keep the winning-token-under-foreign-host case as\n309|   \"no transition\". Add narrowing rows.\n310|3. **E1 — create-row negatives at the engine:** control/expired/foreign-lease\n311|   authorization, stale generation, headless-from-`absent` without\n312|   `headless_creation`, and create's second-effect committed timeout —\n313|   asserting no receipt is bound in the pre-effect cases. Re-key the harness\n314|   rows `N-engine-auth-entry` / `N-engine-generation-entry` so that a mutant\n315|   exempting `create` is killed.\n316|4. **E2 — recheck at every position and the session axis:** rotate the lease\n317|   and the generation before the third stop effect; drift the reported session\n318|   on both status lookup paths (and each of the other five axes, P3-5).\n319|5. P3-1 (pre-link store failure restores the source), P3-2 (fencing sources or\n320|   a stated bound), P3-3 (deadline instant on both entries), P3-4 (`attach`,\n321|   `none` in the kind negatives), P3-6/P3-7 as you see fit; document\n322|   `holder_host_id` as unbound.\n323|6. Reword TRACEABILITY rows 70/71 and the results/LOGBOOK \"recovers through\n324|   status\" once (1) is in; keep everything else as is — the rest of the leaf\n325|   holds.\n326|\n327|Verdict recorded by RUN-260918-4f5cc1; no product edits, commits, checkpoints\n328|or integration were performed; the isolated copies are deleted after\n329|attachment. `commit_ack` is not supplied.","final_result":true}}}
