discipline with the epoch bound witnessed at 1,\n25|  9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values; every\n26|  engine operation's authorization requirement is a checked object\n27|  (`CheckAuthorization`: kind, expiry, lease identity, lease epoch).\n28|- (2) The closed `RetryDisposition` enum (4 members) carried by every\n29|  result, plus the request/result identity contract\n30|  (`MutationContext`/`MutationResult`, `CheckResult` repetition arms,\n31|  per-row idempotency material through landed `IdempotencyKey`).\n32|- (3) The state-entry rules in `Engine`: receipt before first effect,\n33|  source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` on\n34|  unprovable post-commit errors (never `absent`), `creating` only via\n35|  `create`, `quiescing` only via `quiesce-input`, `stale_fenced` only\n36|  via `ObserveFencing` (landed `fencing` park vocabulary, restore\n37|  operation: launch-class is load-bearing, measured by\n38|  `N-fencing-operation`), per-effect auth+generation rechecks,\n39|  deadline cancels waiting never committed effects.\n40|- (4) The canonical `backend_generation` string[1..256] bound in\n41|  every owned surface (0/257 refuse, 256 admits, characters not\n42|  bytes), with staleness refusing the landed\n43|  `terminal_backend_stale_generation` class; bound verdicts agree\n44|  with landed `GenerationDigest` on the boundary corpus.\n45|- (5) The status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary and request-stop\n46|  rows (sources, targets, effects, key material, evidence\n47|  capabilities, exact refusal sets with outside-set rejection via\n48|  landed `CheckErrorAllowed`), plus the create receipt rule.\n49|\n50|Which existing type or gate each addition extends is tabulated in\n51|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md` (Landed extensions); no\n52|second state machine, enum, fencing model, or JSON discipline was\n53|forked.\n54|\n55|This run inherited the rev1 worktree delta verbatim (rev1 never\n56|reached a reviewer: its suite stopped a