 fuzz ×1 | 0 |\n131|| 12–15 | canonicaljson fuzz ×4 | 0 ×4 |\n132|| 16–23 | secconftest fuzz ×8 | 0 ×8 |\n133|| 24 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (contracts=64, cases=140, clauses 56/569 — trunk figures unchanged) |\n134|| 25 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0, tree unmodified |\n135|| 26 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n136|| 27 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n137|| 28 | `git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` | 0 |\n138|| 29 | `task-board validate` | 0 (184 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY issues on unrelated elements; zero name this task or story) |\n139|| 30 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n140|\n141|Full logs in `cmd/` inside\n142|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`. The `.go` tree was\n143|verified byte-identical before and after the race gate\n144|(`go-sha-before-race.txt` == `go-sha-after-race.txt`), so the race\n145|ran against the exact candidate.\n146|\n147|## Files changed\n148|\n149|- `internal/terminstance/` (new package, untracked):\n150|  `doc.go`, `errors.go`, `auth.go`, `disposition.go`, `proof.go`,\n151|  `context.go`, `status.go`, `bodies.go`, `result.go`, `store.go`,\n152|  `fencing.go`, `execute.go`, `mutant_harness.py`,\n153|  `TRACEABILITY.md`, plus 15 test files.\n154|- `internal/axpane/decide.go`: P3-6 doc sentence (comment-only).\n155|- `README.md`: package section (additive).\n156|- `LOGBOOK.md`: leaf entry (additive, newest-first).\n157|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n158|\n159|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n160|\n161|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added.\n162|Binding-object parsing, CLI Result 4, attach/restore/terminate-stale\n163|operations, full create body, credential conditionals, lesser-of\n164|timeout enforcement, and terminal events are stated bounds (see\n165|TRACEABILITY.md). The per-code disposition mapping and the AX-side\n166|seam emission codes are the leaf's contract where the spec pins the\n167|vocabulary but not the mapping.\n168|\n169|## Handoff\n170|\n171|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n172|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n173|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`,\n174|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md`,\n175|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
