{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c66d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b28c-5604-75c0-aae6-73b3ca1e890f"},"sequence":401,"recorded_at":1780531400000797,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d8b3c488-a0a9-443b-8e40-610c9c2591de"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b28d-b357-76e2-ba71-fbe2cf36a39d"},"task_id":"01a0b28d-b357-76e2-ba71-fbe2cf36a39d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b28d-b357-76e2-ba71-fbe2cf36a39d","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/execute.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"time\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// Backend is the modeled terminal backend caller: side-effect execution\n13|// and status observation. No tmux/ConPTY process control and no provider\n14|// process exist behind it; tests model success, coded row refusals,\n15|// uncoded failures and crashes through this interface.\n16|type Backend interface {\n17|\t// PerformEffect executes one side effect and reports its evidence\n18|\t// ID. A nil error proves the commit; a *Error with a row code\n19|\t// proves the backend refused before committing; any other error\n20|\t// proves nothing, not even non-commit.\n21|\tPerformEffect(ctx context.Context, effect terminalbackend.SideEffect) (string, error)\n22|\t// ObserveStatus reports the backend's current observation for one\n23|\t// status body. An error is unknown, never absent.\n24|\tObserveStatus(ctx context.Context, body StatusBody) (StatusObservation, error)\n25|}\n26|\n27|// StatusObservation is the backend-reported status observation: the\n28|// reported state and match verdict, the reported identity tuple the\n29|// engine compares against the query, and the reported capability and\n30|// last-operation facts the landed CheckStatusResult validates.\n31|type StatusObservation struct {\n32|\tState             terminalbackend.InstanceState\n33|\tIdentityMatch     bool\n34|\tWrapperPresent    bool\n35|\tProviderPresent   *bool\n36|\tAttachable        bool\n37|\tLastOperationID   *string\n38|\tLastEffect        *terminalbackend.SideEffect\n39|\tEvidenceIDs       []string\n40|\tProviderRequested bool\n41|\tProviderEvidenced bool\n42|\tAttachEvidenced   bool\n43|\tSessionID         string\n44|\tInstanceID        string\n45|\tBackendID         string\n46|\tImplVersion       string\n47|\tProtoVersion      string\n48|\tGeneration        string\n49|}\n50|\n51|// StatusReport is the validated status outcome: the adopted observation.\n52|// Status performs no transition bookkeeping of its own — no receipt, no\n53|// effects, no before/after — so the report carries the single adopted\n54|// state verbatim.\n55|type StatusReport struct {\n56|\tState           terminalbackend.InstanceState\n57|\tIdentityMatch   bool\n58|\tWrapperPresent  bool\n59|\tProviderPresent *bool\n60|\tAttachable      bool\n61|\tLastOperationID *string\n62|\tLastEffect      *terminalbackend.SideEffect\n63|\tEvidenceIDs     []string\n64|}\n65|\n66|// EngineHooks arms the engine seams tests observe: AfterReceipt fires\n67|// after the durable receipt commits and before the first side effect,\n68|// carrying the interim state (creating for create, the source\n69|// otherwise); BeforeEffect and AfterEffect bracket each committed\n70|// attempt. Hooks observe only: they return nothing and cannot alter\n71|// the outcome.\n72|type EngineHooks struct {\n73|\tAfterReceipt func(operation terminalbackend.Operation, key string, interim terminalbackend.InstanceState)\n74|\tBeforeEffect func(effect terminalbackend.SideEffect)\n75|\tAfterEffect  func(effect terminalbackend.SideEffect)\n76|}\n77|\n78|// Engine executes the §4.C operation rows. Store is the durable receipt\n79|// table; Backend the modeled backend; CurrentLease and CurrentGeneration\n80|// re-read the winning lease and the validated binding generation at\n81|// every check point (function values, never snapshots, so a rotation\n82|// between entry and any effect is caught); Now is the clock. Hooks may\n83|// be nil.\n84|type Engine struct {\n85|\tStore             *ReceiptStore\n86|\tBackend           Backend\n87|\tCurrentLease      func() LeaseView\n88|\tCurrentGeneration func() string\n89|\tNow               func() time.Time\n90|\tHooks             *EngineHooks\n91|}\n92|\n93|// InterimState is the observable state between the durable idempotency\n94|// receipt and the first side effect: creating for create, the source\n95|// state for every other engine operation. creating is entered only by\n96|// create, only after its receipt and before its first listed effect.\n97|func InterimState(operation terminalbackend.Operation, source terminalbackend.InstanceState) terminalbackend.InstanceState {\n98|\tif operation == terminalbackend.OperationCreate {\n99|\t\treturn terminalbackend.StateCreating\n100|\t}\n101|\treturn source\n102|}\n103|\n104|// kindFor maps an engine operation to its AXAuthorization kind. The\n105|// force_stale and restore kinds parse but no engine operation requests\n106|// them: terminate-stale and restore recovery belongs to the story's\n107|// final leaf.\n108|func kindFor(operation terminalbackend.Operation) (AuthorizationKind, bool) {\n109|\tswitch operation {\n110|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationCreate:\n111|\t\treturn AuthorizationCreate, true\n112|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput,\n113|\t\tterminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary,\n114|\t\tterminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n115|\t\treturn AuthorizationControl, true\n116|\tdefault:\n117|\t\treturn \"\", false\n118|\t}\n119|}\n120|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
